Title: The Choir's Reading
Order: 3
Production Code: 1x03

EXT. HALYARD STATION - OUTER PROMENADE - DAY

AMB: a crowd, and beneath it, chanting that doesn't stop when people pass

Boxed text:

"The Kindled Choir doesn't ask permission to set up camp. Their tents are already staked out along the promenade's far end, and the chanting under the station's ambient noise hasn't paused since you arrived."

[[Yevet Sarn]] intercepts the party directly — she's clearly been told who they are.

YEVET SARN
You're carrying something that isn't yours to carry lightly.

If the party shows or mentions [[the Chord Key]], read the following. If they don't, Sarn presses regardless — she already knows.

YEVET SARN (CONT'D)
(taking it carefully, reverently)
This pattern — we have fragments of this exact sequence translated off the Loom's outer inscriptions. It isn't decoration. It's a countdown.

SFX: a low resonant hum from the Key, audible only now

GM note: this is [[the Choir's reading of the Key|the-choirs-reading]] — mark it tentative in play; Sarn's interpretation is doctrine, not confirmed fact, and the table shouldn't be able to tell the difference yet.

YEVET SARN (CONT'D)
The Unveiling doesn't wait for anyone's license or anyone's profit margin, Captain. Whatever you're being paid to find out there, you should already be afraid of the answer.

[[Iyoha Sten]] arrives partway through, flanked by two Compact officers, visibly trying to keep this from becoming a scene.

IYOHA STEN
Marshal. Not on my promenade.

YEVET SARN
(already withdrawing, unbothered)
Your promenade won't matter in a week, Commodore.

Sten watches her go, then turns to the party with the particular exhaustion of someone doing three jobs at once.

IYOHA STEN
Whatever that was about — I'd like to know before the Choir does something about it. Whatever "it" turns out to be.

GM note — contingencies: if the party is openly hostile or violent toward Sarn or the Choir camp here, don't escalate to combat on the promenade — Sten's officers step in first. Treat it instead as accelerating the Choir's posture in `1x05`'s tracked_fields by one step ahead of schedule.
